1020: Whale bug bounty WHALE Home Reporting Terms of Use ENG Open Language Selection ENG KOR Whale Security Bug Bounty Program Naver Corporation launches the Whale Security Bug Bounty Program to encourage security researchers to help us find and fix security vulnerabilities on Whale and to reward their efforts spent to make our product secure. Whale Security Bug Bounty Program ※ As of November 14, 2025, Whale Bug Bounty submissions have moved to the NAVER Bug Bounty platform. Please submit Security bugs via the NAVER Bug Bounty platform. 1. Introduction Naver Corporation launches the Whale Security Bug Bounty Program to encourage security researchers in helping us to find and fix security vulnerabilities on Whale and to reward their efforts spent to make our product secure. 2. Scope We focus on bugs in the latest version of Whale browser. - The bugs must be reproducible on the latest version in the time of reporting - Bugs in third party libraries used by only Whale (not Chromium) are eligible - Bugs in synchronization are eligible Vulnerabilities in other applications or services, including the followings, are NOT eligible. - All of Naver web services are out-of-scope (e.g. &ast;.naver.com, &ast;.navercorp.com) - Web servers communicating with built-in extensions (e.g. Papago, Belli) are out-of-scope - URL preview spoofing in status bar is out-of-scope - Bypassing XSS Auditor is out-of-scope - Vulnerabilities In "IETab" extension - False positive and False negative of the SafeBrowsing feature are out-of-scope 3. Reward Amounts Reward Amounts Vulnerability Examples Maximum Rewards Sandbox Escape File system access, Arbitrary external program execution USD &dollar;7,500 Remote Code Execution Arbitrary code execution using memory corruption bugs without sandbox escape USD &dollar;5,000 Same Origin Policy Violation Universal XSS USD &dollar;4,000 Information Leak Arbitrary memory read USD &dollar;2,000 Protection Bypass Bypassing malicious program download protection, Bypassing malicious page blocks USD &dollar;750 Spoofing on desktop Address bar spoofing, Referer spoofing USD &dollar;500 Others XSS in built-in extensions, other vulnerabilities USD &dollar;500 - We decide the final reward amount based on quality of the report and severity of the vulnerability - We may pay reduced reward amounts if the vulnerability requires complex user interactions - We may pay reduced reward amounts if the vulnerability is introduced by a third party - We can pay higher reward amounts for new class of vulnerability types or clever exploitation techniques 4. Ineligible Submissions We do not pay cash rewards for the following cases - Any bugs reproducible in other Chromium-based browsers which use the same release - Any bugs in operating systems or hardwares - Bugs not reproducible on the latest version - Bugs that are already reported by other participant, or aware by internal reviews - Public bugs - Theoretical vulnerabilities without proof of concept - Simple crash by an assertion or Denial-of-Service (DoS) attack - Requiring too much complex user interactions - Vulnerabilities occured when manually disabling security features - Bugs in experimental features (whale://flags) - Bugs that are already reported to third parties - Bugs that require a user device takeover - Bugs that require downloading or installing a malicious binary file on the device - Bugs that cause a temporary spoofing of the address bar during page loading - Bugs that enable spoofing of UI elements other than the address bar - Bugs that allow spoofing in mobile environments 5. Restrictions and Disclosure Policy - Do not disclose the details of the vulnerability until we fix the vulnerability and the fix is released to most users - Do not engage in any activity that would be disruptive or damaging to other users - Naver employees cannot participate this program 6. Reporting Bugs Please submit your report via this form . Please give us the following information if available: - 