## Manifest 
We distinguish a sidebar extension from ordinary extension by existence of the `sidebar_action` property in the manifest file. 
```javascript
{
  ...
  "sidebar_action": {
    "default_icon": {                      // required 
      "16": "images/icon16.png"
    },
    "default_page": "popup.html",          // required
    "default_title": "Sidebar Extension",   // optional; shown in tooltip
    "use_navigation_bar": true,      // optional; true is default
    "mobile_user_agent": true        // [NOT IMPLEMENTED YET] optional; true is default
  }
  ... 
}
```

* `default_icon` is the icon to launch the sidebar extension. 

![854ab8a52ad9.PNG](https://github.com/naver/whale-developers/blob/master/docs/34650d96-080e-11e7-815c-854ab8a52ad9.png)

* `default_page` is the local resource path to the initial page of the extension.
* `default_title` is the string shown as the tool tip.

![f0d550f01d6e.png](https://github.com/naver/whale-developers/blob/master/docs/fec442d6-080f-11e7-9a1c-f0d550f01d6e.png)

* `use_navigation_bar` is the flag whether the navigation bar is turned on or off, default is true. When you are not using the navigation bar, you must be aware of that your extension page may be navigated to other websites from drag events. To avoid this matter, please refer to [How to avoid my extension from changing urls.](https://github.com/naver/whale-developers/wiki/How-to-avoid-my-extension-from-changing-urls)

![4afddeff04f8.png](https://github.com/naver/whale-developers/blob/master/docs/253a55b2-0fc8-11e7-9b7d-4afddeff04f8.png)

* `mobile_user_agent` is weather the extension panel provides mobile or desktop user agent, default is true
if set true the UA will be 
```
Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 5.0; Nexus 5 Build/WHALE) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Whale/0.7.31.0 Mobile Safari/537.36 sidebar
```
otherwise
```
Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Whale/0.7.30.0 Safari/537.36 sidebar
```
versions numbers may vary.

## types
### [ColorArray](https://developer.chrome.com/extensions/browserAction#type-ColorArray)
### [ImageDataType](https://developer.chrome.com/extensions/pageAction#type-ImageDataType) 


## methods
### **show**
```javascript
whale.sidebarAction.show(integer windowId, object details, function callback); 
```
* Opens the sidebar and gives focus to extension panel. If sidebar is already opened, give focus to extension panel.
* Parameters
  - integer **windowId** (optional) - id of the targeted window. If not defined, targets current window.
  - object **details** (optional) - 
    - string **url** (optional) - url to load in extension panel, if not defined loads the default page
    - boolean **reload** (optional) - when the requested url and current url is identical, reload extension if set to true, default is false
  - function **callback** (optional) - callback parameter should be a function that looks like this:
  ```javascript
  function (integer windowId) {
  }
  ```

### **hide**
```javascript
whale.sidebarAction.hide(integer windowId, function callback);
```
* Closes sidebar (if only the focus is on the current extension panel).
* Parameters
  - integer **windowId** (optional) - id of the targeted window. If not defined, targets current window.
  - function **callback** (optional) - callback parameter should be a function that looks like this:
  ```javascript
  function (integer windowId) {
  }
  ```

### **setTitle**
```javascript
whale.sidebarAction.setTitle(object details);
```
* Sets the title of the sidebar action. This is displayed in a tooltip over the sidebar action. This affects all the other windows at the same time.
* Parameters
  - object **details**
    - string **title**

### **getTitle**
```javascript
whale.sidebarAction.getTitle(function callback);
```
* Retrieves the title of the sidebar action. 
  - function **callback** - callback parameter should be a function that looks like this:
  ```javascript
  function (String result) { ...  }
  ```

### **setIcon**
```javascript
whale.sidebarAction.setIcon(object details);
```
