## Lead 1: Sidebar context SOP bypass — new variant post-CVE-2025-69235

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 | **YES** — Sidebar is a Whale-only feature (in-scope: "Whale browser - latest version") |
| Q2 | **YES** — Any webpage can trigger sidebarAction.show() if extension is installed; content_scripts match ALL origins |
| Q3 | **YES** — SOP bypass → cross-origin data theft (credentials, CSRF tokens); High impact |
| Q4 | **NO** — No passive proof exists. Wiki docs + sample manifest confirm the API shape but do NOT demonstrate a bypass. CVE-2025-69235 was fixed; no evidence the fix is incomplete. "Inspect manifest for use_navigation_bar defaults" is not proof of a vulnerability. |
| Q5 | **UNKNOWN** — Claimed as "new variant" but zero demonstration; could be fixed, could be new — no evidence either way |
| Q6 | **PASS** — Not on always-rejected list |
| Q7 | **NO** — Purely speculative variant hunting with no demonstration on v4.38.386.14 |

**Verdict: INVALID** — Fails Q4: no passive proof; "wiki docs show it exists" ≠ "wiki docs show it's vulnerable." Recurring hypothesis without evidence across 5 models × 20+ runs is not cumulative proof.

---

## Lead 2: Whale sync passphrase KDF weakness / plaintext-adjacent key storage

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 | **YES** — Synchronization explicitly in scope |
| Q2 | **YES (local)** — Local attacker or infostealer with profile access |
| Q3 | **YES** — Weak KDF or plaintext-adjacent storage → decrypt synced passwords/bookmarks → full-account compromise |
| Q4 | **NO** — Binary acquisition is blocked (Cloudflare 403 on APKMirror/apkpure; cloudfront CDN DNS blocked in-sandbox). Prior runs extracted strings but NOT KDF constants/iteration counts. "Grep for PBKDF2/scrypt constants" requires binary access that is not achievable passively here. |
| Q5 | **UNKNOWN** — No evidence of weakness; Android sync encryption added 2025-04 (late, possibly custom) but no demonstration |
| Q6 | **PASS** — Not on always-rejected list |
| Q7 | **NO** — High-confidence hypothesis (58) but zero proof; entirely speculative without binary analysis |

**Verdict: INVALID** — Fails Q4: binary acquisition is blocked in-sandbox; KDF constants/iteration counts remain unextracted; no demonstration of actual weakness. "Vendor says passphrase never leaves device" confirms architecture, not vulnerability.

---

## Lead 3: Dual-tab environment SOP/CSP bypass — new variant post-CVE-2025-62585

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 | **YES** — Dual-tab is a Whale-only feature (in-scope) |
| Q2 | **YES** — Any webpage in dual-tab context |
| Q3 | **YES** — SOP/CSP bypass → credential theft, CSRF exfiltration |
| Q4 | **NO** — Requires HUMAN_ONLY (install browser + dual-tab testing); no passive-first path |
| Q5 | **UNKNOWN** — No variant demonstrated; "8 months since fix" is not evidence of regression |
| Q6 | **PASS** — Not on always-rejected list |
| Q7 | **NO** — Same pattern as Lead 1: speculative variant hunting, no evidence |

**Verdict: INVALID** — Fails Q4: HUMAN_ONLY with no passive proof path. Recurring CVE history signals systemic weakness but does not constitute a new finding without demonstration.

