## Lead 4: Extension API message handling / origin validation bypass

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 | **YES** — whale.* extension API is Whale-only |
| Q2 | **YES** — content_scripts match ALL origins; any webpage can sendMessage |
| Q3 | **YES** — Arbitrary JS execution in extension context → session theft, browser-level API access |
| Q4 | **NO** — Sample background.js calls sidebarAction.show() without documented origin validation, but absence of documented validation ≠ absence of actual validation. Requires live browser testing to prove bypass. |
| Q5 | **PARTIAL** — CVE-2022-24072 and CVE-2024-40618 are fixed; new variant unproven |
| Q6 | **PASS** — Not on always-rejected list |
| Q7 | **NO** — "No documented origin validation" is not "origin validation bypass demonstrated" |

**Verdict: INVALID** — Fails Q4: sample code shows API usage, not a vulnerability. Historical CVEs are fixed; no new variant demonstrated.

