| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 | **YES** — "Third-party libraries used ONLY by Whale (not Chromium)" explicitly in scope |
| Q2 | **Depends** — Would require exploiting the outdated lib |
| Q3 | **YES** — Outdated lib with public exploit → compromise |
| Q4 | **NO** — No bundled library manifest exists publicly; repo is documentation-only; binary extraction required but blocked |
| Q5 | **UNKNOWN** — No inventory built; no comparison possible |
| Q6 | **PASS** — Not on always-rejected list |
| Q7 | **NO** — Entirely speculative; "historical installer bugs exist" does not mean current ones do |

**Verdict: INVALID** — Fails Q4: no inventory, no comparison, no evidence. Pure conjecture.

