## Lead 6: Sync bootstrap-token storage / per-account migration — Whale-only prefs deviation

| Q | Answer |
|---|--------|
| Q1 | **YES** — Synchronization in scope; binary is in-scope asset |
| Q2 | **YES (local)** — Profile access → decrypt sync data |
| Q3 | **YES** — Plaintext bootstrap token in Preferences → full sync decryption |
| Q4 | **NO** — Prior runs confirmed Whale-only prefs keys exist (sync.encryption_bootstrap_token_per_account, whale_need_encryption_key_forced_time) but did NOT extract whether the token is stored plaintext vs OSCrypt-encrypted. Binary re-acquisition blocked. |
| Q5 | **UNKNOWN** — Prefs keys confirmed novel (absent from upstream Chromium) but storage format unverified |
| Q6 | **PASS** — Not on always-rejected list |
| Q7 | **NO** — Strongest lead architecturally but zero proof of actual plaintext storage |

**Verdict: INVALID** — Fails Q4: binary blocked; storage format (plaintext vs encrypted) unverified. "Whale-only prefs key exists" ≠ "prefs key contains plaintext secret." This is the closest to a valid lead but remains unproven.

