<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0,minimum-scale=1.0,maximum-scale=1.0,user-scalable=no">
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Whale Sidebar Extension</title>
  <link href="css/style.css" type="text/css" rel="stylesheet"/>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="header">Whale Sidebar Extension Test</div>

    <div class="section">
      <div class="title">sidebarAction.show() /<br> sidebarAction.hide()</div>
      <div class="description">
        If you want to open or hide sidebar from some action from the web content,
        you can call show() and hide() method using content scripts and background scripts.
        Refer to contentscript.js and backgorund.js.
        Test buttons are injected to all website to test this feature.
      </div>
      <div class="image">
        <img src="img/img01.png" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <div class="title">sidebarAction.getTitle() /<br> sidebarAction.setTitle()</div>
      <div class="description">
        You can update or retrieve the tooltip text using setTitle() and getTitle() method,
        Refer to index.js. Test buttons are available below:
      </div>
      <div class="buttons">
        <button id="setTitle1">Set title to 'ABC'</button>
        <button id="setTitle2">Reset title</button>
      </div>
      <div class="image">
        <img src="img/img02.png" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <div class="title">
        sidebarAction.setBadgeText() /<br>
        sidebarAction.getBadgeText()
      </div>
      <div class="description">
        You can update or retrieve the badge text or badge background color using
        setBadgeText(), getBadgeText(), setBadgeBackgroundColor(), getBadgeBackgroundColor() method.
        Refer to index.js. Test buttons are available below:
      </div>
      <div class="buttons">
        <button id="setBadgeText1">Update badge text and color</button>
        <button id="setBadgeText2">Reset badge</button>
      </div>
      <div class="image">
        <img src="img/img03.png" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <div class="title">
        sidebarAction.onClicked
      </div>
      <div class="description">
        sidebarAction.onClicked.addListener() is used to listen to the extension icon click events.
        The result callback passes the window id and boolean flag whether the sidebar is opened or closed.
        Refer to index.js. Event log:
      </div>
      <div id="clicklog" class="log">
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <script src="js/index.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
</body>
</html>
